 - **Terminal profile** — A named shell command a terminal can launch. Stored host-wide in daemon config as `terminalProfiles`. UI: "Terminal profiles". Code: `TerminalProfile` (`packages/protocol/src/messages.ts:135`), `resolveTerminalProfiles` (`packages/protocol/src/terminal-profiles.ts`). Also selectable as a New Workspace launch target, where the alternative is the chat agent.
 - **Provider** — Agent backend (Claude Code, Codex, Copilot, OpenCode, Pi, Oh My Pi). UI: "Provider". Code: `ProviderSnapshotEntry` (`packages/protocol/src/messages.ts:198`).
 - **Hook** — A plugin lifecycle handler registered with `server.addHook`, named `subject.operation.position` with `before` or `after`; each hook declares whether Paseo waits. See [hooks](../../public-docs/plugins/hooks.md).
